-SR-102,Typed dual-plan state machine,SN-024;SN-006,"plan_round.py shall enforce the typed dual-plan state machine, spend ledger, one-repair and revision caps, position-swap agreement, and PAGE outcomes.",Realizes SN-024;SN-006 by isolating one independently reviewable obligation formerly carried by SR-066.,Happy path selects within budget; illegal repeats raise caps; repair and revision rules hold; arbiter instability or exhaustion pages; state survives JSON round trip.,,S,Test,Verified,4,Dual-plan decomposition,
-SR-103,Allowlist-only dual-plan briefs,SN-024;SN-006,"plan_briefs.py shall assemble planner, critic, and arbiter briefs only from SR/IF registries and strict prompt-template filling.",Realizes SN-024;SN-006 by isolating one independently reviewable obligation formerly carried by SR-066.,"Briefs contain allowlisted registry material, exclude status/log/self-assessment data, reject unknown or unfilled slots, and honor override then kit fallback.",,S,Test,Verified,4,Dual-plan decomposition,
-SR-104,Dual-plan coverage-step adapter,SN-024;SN-006,"plan_coverage_step.py shall adapt mechanical coverage results into clean, implicated-repair, repeated-failure, and malformed round outcomes.",Realizes SN-024;SN-006 by isolating one independently reviewable obligation formerly carried by SR-066.,"Exit 0 advances, first findings implicate and repair once, repeated findings page, malformed is distinct and fails closed, and report payload is captured.",,S,Test,Verified,4,Dual-plan decomposition,
-SR-105,Stable dual-plan artifacts and WI filing,SN-024;SN-006,plan_artifacts.py shall persist stable round artifacts and file selected queued child WIs with mapped predecessors and registry-valid fields.,Realizes SN-024;SN-006 by isolating one independently reviewable obligation formerly carried by SR-066.,"Round ids and stage names are stable; selected rows receive sequential ids, mapped dependencies, empty Deliverables and valid specs/tiers; line endings and prior log content survive.",,S,Test,Verified,4,Dual-plan decomposition,
-SR-106,Fresh-session dual-plan execution,SN-024;SN-006,"plan_runner.py shall run two planners, cross-critiques, bounded revisions, and position-swapped arbiters as fresh sessions and select only on true-plan agreement.",Realizes SN-024;SN-006 by isolating one independently reviewable obligation formerly carried by SR-066.,"The complete round runs unattended with fresh session identities; runtime fallback is bounded; content agreement selects; position bias, missing rubric, or no route pages honestly.",,S,Test,Verified,4,Dual-plan decomposition,
-SR-107,Dual-plan direct-path isolation,SN-024;SN-006,The worker shall refuse a dual row on the direct path.,"Realizes SN-024 and SN-006 — a dual-plan row built by the direct worker skips the competing-plan round that is the whole reason it was marked dual, and the skip is silent. Letting the worker fall back to a single plan was rejected: it produces a plausible result that nobody knows was never contested.",Direct workers reject dual rows and --dual-plan rejects non-dual rows.,,S,Test,Verified,4,Dual-plan decomposition,
-SR-108,Dual-plan round disposition,SN-024;SN-006,"The --dual-plan round shall commit SELECT as a docs-only disposition (children filed as queued specs, validated atomically with their generated views) and surface PAGE per gate policy, never silently.","Realizes SN-024 and SN-016 — a disposition split across commits can land half-applied, and halting every lane for one round's outcome throws away the parallelism for work the outcome does not touch. Applying the disposition per-lane was rejected: the registries are shared, so concurrent writers conflict on every one.",SELECT files children that pass the registry validator; a PAGE preserves the round's evidence on disk.,,S,Test,Verified,4,Dual-plan decomposition,
-SR-109,Spec-lifecycle close-side coherence,SN-002;SN-012,"check_trajectory.py shall flag a done WI whose SpecRef is non-empty and a live docs/specs file (scaffold README/-000 exemplars excluded) cited by no open WI, warning on every run and failing under --strict.","Realizes SN-002 and SN-012 — the open half of the spec-of-record lifecycle was enforced and the close half was not, so a repo accretes stale SpecRefs and orphan live specs (measured at 137 rows and roughly 60 files) until nobody can tell which spec is live. A prose close rule was rejected because it is the control that was already in place while that backlog accumulated: an unenforced rule is indistinguishable from no rule at the point it matters. Opt-in and vacuous on a fresh scaffold.",A done row with a SpecRef and an uncited live spec each produce an R-F WARN with exit 0 on a plain run and exit 1 under --strict; a shared doc cited by any open (incl. deferred/blocked) WI stays clean; docs/specs README and -000 exemplars never flag.,,M,Test,Verified,4,Traceability,
-SR-110,Per-module coverage floors,SN-008;SN-012,"check_coverage.py shall fail when a module listed in the coverage-floor census is below its declared per-module line-coverage percentage in the pytest-cov JSON report, or is absent from that report, so the global --cov-fail-under floor cannot hide a thin high-risk module; an absent report skips and an empty census is a no-op.","Realizes SN-008 and SN-012 — one aggregate coverage number lets well-tested generators subsidize thin coverage at the security and process boundaries, so a green overstates confidence exactly where it matters most. Raising the single global threshold was rejected: it penalizes every module for the weakest one without ever naming it. Opt-in at the product layer, so a non-adopter pays nothing.",A module below its floor exits 1 naming it; a declared module absent from the report exits 1; all floors holding exits 0; no coverage report (e.g. the smoke tier) SKIPs; an absent or empty census is a clean no-op; a malformed floor line fails loudly.,,S,Test,Verified,1,Coverage floors,
-SR-111,Kit-version stamp,SN-001;SN-007,"bootstrap.py shall stamp docs/kit-version with the kit commit SHA and date, marked -dirty on an uncommitted kit tree.","Realizes SN-007 — without a recorded origin an adopter cannot tell which kit version they are on, so a re-sync degrades from a diff into a guess and the ADOPTING.md re-sync procedure has no baseline to diff against. Deriving the version from file hashes was rejected: it reports that something differs without saying from what.",docs/kit-version records the kit SHA and date; a scaffold from an uncommitted kit tree is marked -dirty.,,M,Test,Verified,1,Scaffold generation,
-SR-112,Checked per-agent skill fan-out,SN-012;SN-021,"The per-agent skill copies (.claude/.gemini/.agents) shall be a checked, generated fan-out of the one neutral skills/ source.","Realizes SN-021 — one skill maintained in three agent-specific copies rots into three different skills, and the copy an agent actually loads is the one nobody edited. Maintaining a single shared directory was rejected because each agent harness looks in its own path; the fan-out is forced, so the copies are generated and drift is a finding.",A per-agent copy that diverges byte-for-byte from source is detectable and refreshed by one command.,,C,Test,Verified,1,Skills index + fan-out,
-SR-113,Dev-setup wires the process floor,SN-001,dev-setup shall wire the pre-commit process floor (core.hooksPath) from its baseline.,"Realizes SN-001 — a process floor that needs a separate opt-in step is active only for the contributors who already knew about it, which is the reverse of what a floor is for. Documenting the git command was rejected: the floor then protects the rung the contributor read about rather than the one they actually run.",After dev-setup the pre-commit floor is active without a separate setup step.,,S,Test,Verified,1,Onboarding + dev-setup,
-SR-114,Kit scripts run across the supported OSes,SN-003;SN-011,"The kit scripts shall run on Python 3.11+ across Linux, Windows and macOS.","Realizes SN-011 — a script that works only where its author ran it turns portability into a defect the adopter finds, and the path, line-ending and locking differences that break it are invisible on a single platform. Testing one platform and reading the others by inspection was rejected: every one of those differences has been a real failure here.","The CI matrix spans Linux, Windows and macOS on Python 3.11 and latest (3.x) and is green; macOS runs on current Python only — the 3.11 floor is a platform-agnostic language/stdlib guarantee already exercised on Linux and Windows, while macOS's job is OS-specific behavior (fcntl.flock, paths, git worktrees) that does not vary by Python version, so the macOS+3.11 cell is excluded as a redundant-coverage call, not a runner-availability workaround (3.11 has arm64 macOS builds).",,M,Analysis,Modified,1,Portability,
-SR-115,Deterministic ready ordering,SN-025;SN-006,"schedule.py shall order the eligible ready frontier deterministically by gate class, then Priority descending, then transitive downstream-dependent count descending, then remaining hard-path length descending, then WI id.","Realizes SN-025 — a frontier that is correct but unordered lets two readers of the same registry dispatch different work, so a rerun stops being reproducible and a scheduling bug cannot be replayed. Ordering by WI id alone was rejected: it ignores the critical path, so the chain everything waits on gets picked last.",Ordering is identical across --explain and --format json; Priority outranks downstream-dependent count within one gate class; simulate --jobs 1 matches the serial order.,,M,Test,Modified,4,Parallel dispatch,
-SR-116,Generated status surface,SN-025;SN-010,The trunk lane shall maintain docs/status.md's generated snapshot as a freshness-gated reference surface never written on a worker branch (trunk_step --regen; concurrency-restructure SS5.2). (The docs/run-state half of this row retired with the dispatcher at Phase 5.),"Realizes SN-010 — an agent-authored status surface drifts from the state it reports and is trusted anyway, and a worker branch writing it makes the snapshot describe one lane instead of the project. Letting each worker append its own status was rejected: it produces a file that conflicts on every integration and reports no coherent whole.",The status snapshot regenerates on the trunk after a merge and fails its freshness gate when stale; work branches skip the gate and never commit the artifact.,,M,Test,Modified,4,Parallel dispatch,
-SR-117,Superseded: Atomic traincar reservation and lane leasing,SN-025;SN-016,"SR-117 is superseded by SR-132 (concurrency-restructure Phase 5, 2026-07-29): the bespoke dispatcher/reservation machinery this specified was deleted outright — git plus the serial local integrator is the integration seam (claims are serial trunk commits, the composed tree is the candidate by construction, recovery is plain git history). Active requirements, implementation links, and decomposition evidence shall cite the replacement row.","Identity history for the Phase 5 deletion (the SS6 fate table): the requirement's job survives in the integration seam, its machinery does not.",The SupersededBy link resolves to SR-132; no LLR cites this row; TC-133 cites it.,,M,Inspection,Verified,4,Parallel dispatch,SR-132
